The guard checks `GateResult.command`. LAN workers redact results before returning them (~src/workers/client.ts:781), and land matches the check after normalization (~src/land/queue.ts:858). So terminal-sequence normalization can remove compound syntax before recognition. For example, `bun test <ESC>]0; security-scan #<BEL>` normalizes to `bun test `. Review reproduced this through a simulated LAN result: worker validation accepted it, the targeted retry ran and the land reached `landed`.

Fix: run the single-invocation check on the selected check's own command from the trusted configuration, after docs-only selection (the `check` that `retryFailures` already receives with each failure), as well as on the returned command. One implementation for every targeted-only caller.

